  "title": "Mother's side",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "On your **mother's side**:\n\n- **নানা / নানি** — grandfather / grandmother\n- **মামা / মামি** — mother's brother / his wife\n- **খালা / খালু** — mother's sister / her husband\n\nFather's side or mother's side? Listen to the first sound: **দাদা / দাদি** (*da-*) are your father's parents, **নানা / নানি** (*na-*) your mother's.\n\n'Mother's' is **মায়ের** (*mayer*). After most words ending in a vowel the possessive is just -র (বাবা → বাবার), but মা takes **-এর** with a little **য়** glide: মা → মায়ের.\n\n**মামা** is a special word: in Bangladesh it's also how you cheerfully address a rickshaw driver or the man at the tea stall. You'll practise that in Lesson 6.\n\nKolkata: maternal grandparents are দাদু / দিদিমা, mother's sister is মাসি, her husband মেসো.",
